{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals","id":1098707,"title":"Penny Dreadful Tv Show: Characters as Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T02:14:21-07:00","id":1098707,"title":"Penny Dreadful Tv Show: Characters as Supernaturals","content":"I am about to create PD tv show based campaign and use characters as Supernaturals, i'm open to new ideas and suggestions for main characters like Vanessa as a Medium or a Mage(pre-Hollow One maybe), Victor Frankenstein as \u00c6esculpian, Mina as a Setite or Nightcomers as Nephandi... also open to notable stats, merits or flaws","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-22-2020, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:23:30-07:00","id":1098863,"title":"","content":"Based on Vanessa's background I'd say either Verbena or possibly <i>Widderslainte</i> Nephandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:18:33-07:00","id":1098916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1098863#post1098863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on Vanessa's background I'd say either Verbena or possibly <i>Widderslainte</i> Nephandus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But she is very religious and never make a deal with demons, only gets possessed by them to make her suffer and obey to Dark Lord, she resisted. What else she might be? Whats her major demeanor archetype?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T16:36:16-07:00","id":1098939,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think <i>Widderslainte</i> Nephandus fits amazingly well.<br /> <br /> <i>Widderslainte</i> Nephandi are people who made the choice to become Nephandi in their previous life, so they are already born with an inverted Avatar. Even if the Widderslainte himself isn't innately evil (most seem to lean in that direction by default, but not all), he's going to be trapped fighting a losing battle with his own magickal self.<br /> <br /> And that kind of fits with what we see in Vanessa. Vanessa is a good person, and religion gives her a way to fight her darker impulses. At the same time though, her magic powers open her up to possession and violation and have made her the target of cults and supernatural beings who want to possess her. She is more powerful than any other witch in the series, but seems to have a particular affinity for darker magic. Her ability to speak the Devil's Tongue with very little training would support the idea of her being a reincarnated Nephandi. (Especially with the whole Mother of Evil thing.)<br /> <br /> The end of her story fits too. That's probably the happiest ending that a <i>widderslainte</i> can hope to get.<br /> <br /> I'd probably go with some variation of penitent and martyr for her archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T17:29:29-07:00","id":1098945,"title":"","content":"Yeah, reincarnated as already &quot;Dark&quot; explanation fits to her, even tho she is very &quot;Hollow One&quot; like with all those opium tables and mediumship concept...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-22-2020, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:38:53-07:00","id":1099027,"title":"","content":"I could see Vanessa as a Dreamspeaker, especially with a merit like Medium or one of the other no &quot;off switch&quot; ways of seeing the spirit world regardless of use of the Spirit Sphere. Or a Verbena with the Spirit Sight merit and the Dark Fate flaw.<br /> <br /> Victor...honestly, Victor always struck me just a relatively pedestrian sorcerer. He doesn't exhibit the range of a full mage, doesn't really have any innate supernatural powers, just a really good grasp of creating soulless monsters, and that smacks of a sorcery path.<br /> <br /> Ethan...eh, I would probably go with Uktena or Wendigo, as they are the last of the Native American tribes, although I think Stargazer fits better.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Kaetenay would be a Dreamspeaker, I find it kinda hard to think of him as something else.<br /> <br /> Dorian...eh...I would probably use the Mummy rules for him, even though he is more of a damned thing than a Mummy. Or a revenant with the immortal merit from...Mage iirc.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:44:43-07:00","id":1099072,"title":"","content":"Mediumship is available to all known traditions or crafts but her paradigm far from Dreamspeaker or Verbena(Her mentor Joan Clayton might be), she believes in Abrahamic Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-22-2020, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:51:25-07:00","id":1099167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salih Bu\u011fra Algan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1099072#post1099072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mediumship reachable by all known traditions or crafts but her paradigm far from Dreamspeaker or Verbena(Her mentor Joan Clayton might be), she believes in Abrahamic Lore. Spoilers* Kaetenay is literally a Wendigo Garou \ud83d\ude02</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What, exactly stops a Dreamspeaker from believing in Abrahamic lore? As far as paradigm, she deals almost exclusivly in spirits and tweaking with the unseen, kinda points to spirit magic. Maybe Euthanatos, but that gets to be dicey with some of what she does.<br /> <br /> I prefer to look at Kaetenay as a Mage who uses magic to shift, but yeah, if he does the straight up Werewolf thing, Wendigo fits extremely well. Maybe why I don't jump for that option, way to obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:32:51-07:00","id":1099210,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I don't really see the Dreamspeaker angle either. Vanessa's magic tends to be pretty heavily spirit, sure, but there isn't really anything about her methodology or belief system that really suits the Dreamspeakers. She doesn't venerate the spirits that possess her, she quite understandably fears them. There isn't really any evidence of totems or medicine-work in her practice. She's also devoutly Catholic, and while I suppose that it's possible to create a Catholic Dreamspeaker, it doesn't seem terribly likely. The belief systems are pretty diametrically opposed in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> I don't think she easily slots into a Tradition. Her training (through Joan) would be more Verbena based, but her practice leans more toward Hermetic or Hollow One to me. You could arguably make an argument for Celestial Chorister, based on her more religious aspects, but I don't think it fits. She doesn't tend to see her magic as coming directly from God through her, so much as something she does through her own methods. (That's also another reason why Dreamspeaker doesn't really work for me. It's another faith based Tradition, rather than a methodical one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:25:28-07:00","id":1099241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1099210#post1099210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I don't really see the Dreamspeaker angle either. Vanessa's magic tends to be pretty heavily spirit, sure, but there isn't really anything about her methodology or belief system that really suits the Dreamspeakers. She doesn't venerate the spirits that possess her, she quite understandably fears them. There isn't really any evidence of totems or medicine-work in her practice. She's also devoutly Catholic, and while I suppose that it's possible to create a Catholic Dreamspeaker, it doesn't seem terribly likely. The belief systems are pretty diametrically opposed in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> I don't think she easily slots into a Tradition. Her training (through Joan) would be more Verbena based, but her practice leans more toward Hermetic or Hollow One to me. You could arguably make an argument for Celestial Chorister, based on her more religious aspects, but I don't think it fits. She doesn't tend to see her magic as coming directly from God through her, so much as something she does through her own methods. (That's also another reason why Dreamspeaker doesn't really work for me. It's another faith based Tradition, rather than a methodical one.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess a lot of it depends on how you look at traditions. I've played VA technoshamans, very methodical ritual magick style Cultists, and so on. The traditions to me have always been more about a basic worldview, not a straightjacket. So for me, it isn't hard to look at Vanessa and see someone who Awakened to what is, to her, a horrible curse and doing everything she can to make sense of and cope with it. Much more of a personal horror than personal exploration story than we normally see from Mage, but still not completely out of context for WoD. So for me, I would have to either make her a Hollow One (the easy route) a Widderslainte Nephandi (fits, but unless I wanted everything to unfold exactly the way it did in the series, kinda straightjackets her) or try and look at it a little out of the box and go with something like Dreamspeaker. She isn't the typical Dreamspeaker, but she does have some themes in common, and if you focus on her relationship with the unseen, it starts to fit even better. Ditto for the Chorus, if you play up her faith and its role in her life and magickal practice. Euthanatos I could see if you played her acceptance of fate and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:00:58-07:00","id":1099279,"title":"","content":"The thing is that while there is a lot of potential variation within the Traditions, for example it is perfectly reasonable to make a technoshaman Dreamspeaker, there is still a core world view inherent in each Tradition. It has to do with how each one fundamentally views magic and the world<br /> <br /> I think it's a bit funny that you address the Dreamspeakers, Euthanatos and Celestial Chorus, because those are the Traditions that I think are explicitly not applicable to Vanessa. I would consider those &quot;faith-based Traditions.&quot; Specifically, they are Traditions in which religious practice and magickal practice are so intertwined that they are essentially the same thing. It may take a different form for each individual practitioner, but in the end, magic ends up being a reflection of their relationship with either a monotheistic divine, an animistic world, or the veneration of a rebirth cycle.<br /> <br /> Penny Dreadful shows us that Vanessa is religious, but her religious worship is presented as completely separate from her magickal practice. If anything, they're implicitly antithetical. Her magic is what endangers her soul, as it's the reason that she's targeted by so much evil. It's explicitly tied to her past/destiny as the Mother of Evil. She doesn't pray to God for her magic, or with her magic, she begs for protection from her magic and all the baggage that goes with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-01-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:14:18-07:00","id":1099285,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, would Brona or Caliban be more like Risen or the CoD Prometheans? I admit, I don't know much of ANYTHING about the Chronicles of Darkness splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T23:39:03-07:00","id":1099402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1099285#post1099285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially, would Brona or Caliban be more like Risen or the CoD Prometheans? I admit, I don't know much of ANYTHING about the Chronicles of Darkness splats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are they a different person from who they were before becoming what they are now? If so, then Promethean fits. Prometheans are like the Frankenstein's Monster, being usually but in no way always built out of human body parts. They're not resurrected people, although their creators (&quot;demiurges&quot;) and other people who see them might mistakenly believe they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T10:02:33-07:00","id":1099848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1099402#post1099402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are they a different person from who they were before becoming what they are now? If so, then Promethean fits. Prometheans are like the Frankenstein's Monster, being usually but in no way always built out of human body parts. They're not resurrected people, although their creators (&quot;demiurges&quot;) and other people who see them might mistakenly believe they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They are different people. But maybe not. They come across as very Promethean without all the alchemical powers. Where they do think they are who they were it could easily be handled in the place where, in Promethean, it allows for some trace memories of the original to surface. Brona and Adam would definitely be VERY invested in that, but, really they are completely different people than they were when alive in pretty much every way. <br /> <br /> The major point of divergence might be more along the lines of the fact that Brona doesn't really ever revert to looking like she's pieced back together. Brona doesn't seem to inspire Disquiet so much, but Adam sure does. Oh, and in the Supernatural version of the WOD/COD, other supernaturals don't suffer from Disquiet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T21:02:04-07:00","id":1100004,"title":"","content":"Dorian would be someone with a really powerful demonic investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:07:01-07:00","id":1100244,"title":"","content":"I'd go with Ethan being a Silver Fang in terms of what he is not necessarily being a one for one relationship from show to game. It certainly fits the fact he's a wealthy cowboy with poor control over his powers and insanity.<br /> <br /> But also the Chosen Champion of Gaia/God.<br /> <br /> I'd also note that an exorcism is very appropriate for Garou to drive out evil spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T07:07:02-07:00","id":1101960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098707-penny-dreadful-tv-show-characters-as-supernaturals?p=1100004#post1100004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dorian would be someone with a really powerful demonic investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dorian is based to the story of the Giant with the separated soul. Dorian is a monster because he has no soul and thus on Empathy or true Compassion. He could be a failed Mage, a Dauntain (a changeling fallen to the Banality), or a strange twist on a Risen. The last has the most suitable mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}